# Overlay: serve from per-Spark parts instead of the full pack. Run on four Sparks with this launcher at a
# 4,096-token window with the 4-bit drafter (2026-11-22, receipts/parts/launch-4k/); not at 131,072 tokens.
# Each Spark holds PARTS_ROOT/common/ and only its own PARTS_ROOT/rankN/ (N is the Spark's place in RING_HOSTS,
# from 0), as tools/split_ranks.sh cuts them: 79.74 GB per Spark for the 4b6b quant, against 371.84 GB for the
# full pack. The server reads PARTS_ROOT/common. Before it starts, launch/launch.sh checks that each Spark holds
# common/ and its own rankN/ and no other rank's folder (launch/SETTINGS.md, "PARTS_ROOT").
#
# Usage (after your base ring.env and the relay overlay):
#   bash launch/launch.sh --env-file launch/ring.env --env-file launch/ring.relay.env.example --env-file launch/ring.parts.env.example
#
# TF_HY4_TRUNK stays the width the parts were cut with (4b6b in ring.env.example); the engine refuses another.
# The 4-bit drafter is not in the parts. Every Spark needs its folder at the same path, 5 files and 8.57 GB:
# bash tools/drafter_folder.sh FULL_PACK /data/models/hy4-drafter-4b builds it where the full pack is, and
# launch/STAGING.md ("Per-Spark parts") gives how to copy and check the parts and the folder. With it, one Spark
# holds 88.31 GB. To draft with the BF16 drafter inside the parts instead, with no drafter
# folder, use the three commented lines below; that drafter's speed here is not measured.
# The model folder is now common/, so the served name is set to the full pack's ("hy4-exl3" with ring.env.example).

PARTS_ROOT="/data/models/hy4-parts"
MODEL_DIR="${PARTS_ROOT}/common"
DRAFTER_DIR="/data/models/hy4-drafter-4b"
SERVE_MODEL_NAME="hy4-exl3"
# DRAFTER_DIR=""
# TF_HY4_DRAFTER_EXL3=""
# TF_HY4_DRAFTER_HEAD=""
